# 12. MOTION AND INTERACTION DESIGN

Use animation to improve the experience, not to decorate everything.

Motion:
- Navigation transitions.
- Dropdown interactions.
- Subtle section reveals.
- Button interactions.
- Image hover treatments.
- Mobile menu transitions.

GSAP:
- Carefully controlled hero introduction.
- Editorial image reveal.
- Selected scroll-based storytelling.
- Subtle parallax on appropriate photography.

Animation principles:
- Smooth.
- Intentional.
- Subtle.
- Professional.
- Performance-conscious.

Avoid:
- Excessive scroll hijacking.
- Constant floating animations.
- Unnecessary bouncing.
- Overanimated cards.
- Delayed content visibility.
- Animations that interfere with reading.

Respect prefers-reduced-motion.

Do not use GSAP and Motion to animate the same element simultaneously.

